### Description

Support of custom UI fields for custom `SocialIdentityProvider` OR `ClientAuthenticator` implementations in `keycloak.v2` theme. 

### Discussion

_No response_

### Motivation

Custom Identity Providers need more fields than OIDC default ones 
<img width="1036" alt="Screenshot 2023-04-07 at 2 20 50 PM" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/3843966/230666107-4df5ade2-92b4-4a39-b082-5c77222824b0.png">

For instance see this issue https://github.com/klausbetz/apple-identity-provider-keycloak/issues/13. For admin v1 theme this provider has custom template [realm-identity-provider-apple.html](https://github.com/klausbetz/apple-identity-provider-keycloak/blob/main/src/main/resources/theme-resources/resources/partials/realm-identity-provider-apple.html). 

Given that admin v2 theme is based on reactjs there is no way to extend it in theme resources and add additional fields on UI. See [ExtendedFieldsForm.tsx](https://github.com/keycloak/keycloak/blob/main/js/apps/admin-ui/src/identity-providers/component/ExtendedFieldsForm.tsx#L13):

```tsx
export const ExtendedFieldsForm = ({ providerId }: ExtendedFieldsFormProps) => {
  switch (providerId) {
    case "facebook":
      return <FacebookFields />;
    case "github":
      return <GithubFields />;
    case "google":
      return <GoogleFields />;
    case "openshift-v3":
    case "openshift-v4":
      return <OpenshiftFields />;
    case "paypal":
      return <PaypalFields />;
    case "stackoverflow":
      return <StackoverflowFields />;
    case "linkedin":
      return <LinkedInFields />;
    default:
      return null;
  }
};
```

### Details

Latest keycloak 21.0.2 does not support this. In the past it was an option.

### Description

Hello Keycloak team,  

Expose the password policies like "minimum lenght" to the FreeMarker context of the login theme pages.
Example:  

```ts
type KcContext = {
        passwordPolicies?: {
            /** The minimum length of the password */
            length?: number;
            /** The minimum number of digits required in the password */
            digits?: number;
            /** The minimum number of lowercase characters required in the password */
            lowerCase?: number;
            /** The minimum number of uppercase characters required in the password */
            upperCase?: number;
            /** The minimum number of special characters required in the password */
            specialChars?: number;
            /** Whether the password can be the username */
            notUsername?: boolean;
            /** Whether the password can be the email address */
            notEmail?: boolean;
        };
};
```

### Discussion

https://keycloak.discourse.group/t/make-password-policies-available-to-freemarker/11632

### Motivation

By exposing these password policies, login theme authors can provide real-time feedback to users, ensuring that passwords meet the security standards set by the Keycloak server. 

Example:  
<img width="601" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/317a8882-018d-4f96-86ef-0c84a892443a">


### Details

At the moment Keycloakify build themes that includes [this custom extension](https://github.com/jcputney/keycloak-theme-additional-info-extension) in order to make this feature available.  
However the dependency on this Java extension is a problem for some company using Keycloakify.  

Thanks for considering the issue.
